\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Dataset\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The dataset contains EEG-related measurements represented by variables 
\f2\fs26 X1
\f1\fs24  through 
\f2\fs26 X16
\f1\fs24 , along with seizure labels.\
For the binary classification task, the data was divided into:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 5,600 training observations\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 2,400 test observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The analysis also included a second classification task involving four seizure-related categories.\
The original dataset is not included in this repository because it was provided through course materials and is not being redistributed here.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Approach\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 I compared several models throughout the analysis.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

